LIB_LOAD("mx",{"mx1":{"challenge":[{"q":"What did Brother Lawrence call his short sayings?","o":["Maxims","Poems","Songs","Letters"],"why":"Spiritual Maxims."},{"q":"To whom are all things possible, according to the first maxim?","o":["The one who believes","The one who's clever","The one who's rich","Nobody"],"why":"Mark 9:23 too."},{"q":"What did the worried father ask Jesus to help?","o":["His unbelief","His farm","His money","His house"],"why":"\"Help thou mine unbelief.\""},{"q":"What does the maxim say makes things less difficult?","o":["Hope","Fear","Money","Speed"],"why":"Like Abraham."},{"q":"Who \"against hope believed in hope\"?","o":["Abraham","Jacob","Peter","Bisola"],"why":"Romans 4:18."},{"q":"How long did Jacob serve for Rachel?","o":["Seven years","Two years","Forty years","One year"],"why":"It felt like a few days."},{"q":"What makes things easier, according to the maxim?","o":["Love","Shouting","Luck","Tiredness"],"why":"Love lightens the load."},{"q":"\"The greatest of these is...\"","o":["charity","faith","hope","patience"],"why":"1 Corinthians 13:13."},{"q":"What does 'persevere' mean?","o":["Keep going and not give up","Give up quickly","Run fast","Sleep in"],"why":"Easier still for those who persevere."},{"q":"\"Let us not be weary in well...\"","o":["doing","sleeping","eating","talking"],"why":"Galatians 6:9."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What are 'virtues'?","o":["Good qualities like faith, hope and love","Kinds of food","Musical instruments","Old coins"],"why":"The first maxim names three."},"choices":[{"title":"Shaky faith","q":"You're not sure God can really help with a big problem in your family.","o":[{"t":"Pray honestly: 'Lord, I believe; help my unbelief.'","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Bring the faith you have."},{"t":"Don't pray until you feel sure.","f":"The father prayed with shaky faith, and Jesus helped."},{"t":"Pretend you're totally certain.","f":"God wants honesty, not pretending."}]},{"title":"Losing hope","q":"You've been praying for months for a friend who's ill, and you're losing hope.","o":[{"t":"Keep praying and holding on to God's faithfulness, and talk to someone you trust.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Hope holds on, like Abraham."},{"t":"Stop praying.","f":"Against hope, believe in hope."},{"t":"Keep your feelings to yourself.","f":"Share the load with God and a trusted adult."}]},{"title":"Heavy duty","q":"You have to help look after a younger cousin every Saturday. It feels like a chore.","o":[{"t":"Choose to love your cousin and do it for God.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Love makes it easier, like Jacob's seven years."},{"t":"Do it grumpily.","f":"Love turns a burden into joy."},{"t":"Ignore your cousin and use your phone.","f":"Love shows up and pays attention."}]},{"title":"Quitting time","q":"You started reading your Bible daily but stopped after a week.","o":[{"t":"Start again today, and keep going a little each day.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Easier still to the one who perseveres."},{"t":"Give up. You're not a 'Bible person'.","f":"It grows with practice."},{"t":"Wait for next year.","f":"In due season you'll reap, if you faint not."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"cloister","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 1 of Spiritual Maxims in real life."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"✨ Bring the faith you have: 'Lord, I believe; help my unbelief.'"},{"sc":"starsky","n":"⭐ Hope holds on to a faithful God."},{"sc":"field","n":"💗 Love lightens every load."},{"sc":"college","n":"🥁 Keep practising. Don't give up."}],"stops":{"mx1s1":{"story":[{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"Hello again, friends! Besides my conversations and letters, I wrote down some short sayings, called {maxim}s. Here's the first one."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"big","t":"All things are possible to the one who believes. They are less difficult to the one who hopes, easier to the one who loves, and easier still to the one who perseveres in all three."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"Jesus once met a father whose son suffered terrible fits. The disciples had tried to help, but couldn't."},{"sc":"galilee","w":"mxfather","e":"worried","t":"If thou canst do any thing, have compassion on us, and help us."},{"sc":"galilee","w":"mxjesus","e":"smile","t":"If thou canst believe, all things are possible to him that believeth."},{"sc":"galilee","w":"mxfather","e":"worried","t":"Lord, I believe; help thou mine unbelief."},{"sc":"galilee","n":"Jesus healed the boy, took him by the hand, and lifted him up."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"Notice: the father's faith wasn't perfect! He said, 'I believe, but help my unbelief.' Jesus didn't send him away. Bring Him the faith you have, even if it's small and shaky."}],"quote":{"text":"All things are possible to him who believes, less difficult to him who hopes, easier to him who loves, and still more easy to him who perseveres in the practice of these three virtues.","who":"The first of the Spiritual Maxims","tag":"Brother Lawrence's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Bring the faith you have","text":"Brother Lawrence's first maxim says all things are possible to the one who believes. A worried father told Jesus, 'I believe; help my unbelief,' and Jesus healed his son. Your faith doesn't have to be perfect. Bring Him what you have."},"think":"Is there something you find hard to believe God can do? Try praying the father's prayer: 'Lord, I believe; help my unbelief.'","quiz":[{"q":"What is a maxim?","o":["A short, wise saying","A long book","A song","A kind of bread"],"why":"Brother Lawrence wrote many."},{"q":"According to the first maxim, what is possible to the one who believes?","o":["All things","Nothing","Only small things","Only easy things"],"why":"And easier still with hope and love."},{"q":"Who brought his son to Jesus?","o":["A worried father","A king","A soldier","A fisherman"],"why":"The disciples couldn't help."},{"q":"What did the father say to Jesus?","o":["\"Lord, I believe; help thou mine unbelief\"","\"I don't believe\"","\"Go away\"","\"I'm sure\""],"why":"Mark 9:24."},{"q":"Did Jesus send him away because his faith was shaky?","o":["No, He healed the boy","Yes","He told him to come back later","He ignored him"],"why":"Bring the faith you have."}]},"mx1s2":{"story":[{"sc":"starsky","n":"God promised Abraham a son, and more descendants than the stars in the sky. But years passed. Abraham was nearly a hundred, and his wife Sarah was ninety. Still no baby."},{"sc":"starsky","w":"mxabraham","e":"worried","t":"By every human measure, it's impossible. We are far too old."},{"sc":"starsky","w":"mxabraham","e":"smile","t":"But God has promised. And God has never broken a promise. I will keep hoping."},{"sc":"tent","n":"The Bible says Abraham, against hope, believed in hope. And God kept His word: baby Isaac was born, and the whole household laughed for joy!"},{"sc":"home","w":"mxikenna","e":"worried","t":"My dad lost his job three months ago. He's been looking and looking. Sometimes I stop hoping."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"Ikenna, that's why my maxim says things are less difficult for the one who hopes. Hope doesn't pretend everything is fine. It holds on to God, because He's faithful."},{"sc":"home","w":"mxikenna","e":"smile","t":"Then I'll keep praying for Dad, and keep hoping, like Abraham under the stars."}],"quote":{"text":"And being not weak in faith, he considered not his own body now dead, when he was about an hundred years old... He staggered not at the promise of God through unbelief.","who":"Romans 4:19-20","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Hope holds on","text":"Abraham was nearly a hundred, but he kept hoping in God's promise, and Isaac was born. Brother Lawrence said things are less difficult for the one who hopes. Hope doesn't pretend; it holds on to a faithful God."},"think":"What are you hoping and praying for right now? How does Abraham's story encourage you?","quiz":[{"q":"What did God promise Abraham?","o":["A son and descendants like the stars","A palace","Gold","A long holiday"],"why":"But years passed."},{"q":"About how old was Abraham?","o":["Nearly a hundred","Twenty","Forty","Twelve"],"why":"And Sarah was ninety."},{"q":"What does Romans 4:18 say Abraham did?","o":["Against hope believed in hope","Gave up hoping","Forgot God's promise","Laughed at God"],"why":"He held on."},{"q":"What was the name of Abraham's promised son?","o":["Isaac","Joseph","David","Moses"],"why":"The household laughed for joy."},{"q":"What did Ikenna decide to do for his dad?","o":["Keep praying and hoping","Give up","Stop talking to him","Nothing"],"why":"Like Abraham under the stars."}]},"mx1s3":{"story":[{"sc":"field","n":"Long ago, Jacob fell in love with Rachel. Her father, Laban, said Jacob could marry her if he worked for him for seven whole years."},{"sc":"field","n":"Seven years of looking after sheep and goats, in the heat of the day and the cold of the night. That's a long time!"},{"sc":"field","n":"But the Bible says something beautiful: the seven years seemed to Jacob like only a few days, because of the love he had for her."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"big","t":"That's my maxim! Things are easier for the one who loves. When you love God, serving Him stops feeling like a heavy load. It becomes a joy."},{"sc":"home","w":"mxbisola","e":"smile","t":"Like when I carry my baby brother around all afternoon. My arms should get tired, but I love him so much that I hardly notice!"},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"Exactly! I cooked for years, for the love of God. Love turned the kitchen from a burden into a joy."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"Paul said that of faith, hope and love, the greatest is love. And the more we know how much God loves us, the more we love Him back."}],"quote":{"text":"And Jacob served seven years for Rachel; and they seemed unto him but a few days, for the love he had to her.","who":"Genesis 29:20","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Love lightens the load","text":"Seven years of hard work felt like a few days to Jacob, because he loved Rachel. Brother Lawrence said everything is easier for the one who loves. When you love God, serving Him becomes a joy, not a burden."},"think":"What feels like a burden in your life right now? How might love, for God and for others, make it lighter?","quiz":[{"q":"How long did Jacob work to marry Rachel?","o":["Seven years","Seven days","Seventy years","One month"],"why":"Genesis 29:20."},{"q":"How did those years feel to Jacob?","o":["Like a few days","Like forever","Boring","Terrible"],"why":"Because he loved her."},{"q":"What does the maxim say makes things easier?","o":["Love","Money","Fear","Sleep"],"why":"Easier to the one who loves."},{"q":"Who did Bisola carry all afternoon?","o":["Her baby brother","A bag of rice","Her dog","Her friend"],"why":"Love made it light."},{"q":"Which is the greatest of faith, hope and charity?","o":["Charity (love)","Faith","Hope","None"],"why":"1 Corinthians 13:13."}]},"mx1s4":{"story":[{"sc":"college","n":"Bisola wanted to learn the talking drum. The first week, her hands hurt, and she sounded terrible."},{"sc":"college","w":"mxbisola","e":"frown","t":"I'll never be good at this. Maybe I should quit."},{"sc":"college","w":"mxikenna","e":"smile","t":"Remember the end of Brother Lawrence's maxim?"},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"All things are easier still to the one who perseveres. Believing, hoping and loving aren't things you do once. You practise them, day after day, until they become part of you."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"big","t":"Paul said: let us not be weary in well doing, for in due season we shall reap, if we faint not. The harvest comes to those who keep going."},{"sc":"college","n":"Bisola kept practising, a little every day. Three months later, she played at the school cultural day, and everyone clapped along."},{"sc":"college","w":"mxbisola","e":"big","t":"If I can persevere with a drum, I can persevere with God too!"}],"quote":{"text":"Let us run with patience the race that is set before us, looking unto Jesus the author and finisher of our faith.","who":"Hebrews 12:1-2","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Keep going","text":"Bisola nearly quit the talking drum, but kept practising until she could play. Brother Lawrence's maxim ends: things are easier still for the one who perseveres. Faith, hope and love grow by practising them every day."},"think":"What good habit with God have you started and then stopped? How could you start again and keep going?","quiz":[{"q":"What instrument did Bisola want to learn?","o":["The talking drum","The guitar","The violin","The trumpet"],"why":"Her hands hurt at first."},{"q":"What did she want to do in the first week?","o":["Quit","Perform","Buy a new drum","Teach others"],"why":"She sounded terrible."},{"q":"According to the maxim, who finds things easier still?","o":["The one who perseveres","The one who quits","The one who's lucky","The one who's rich"],"why":"In faith, hope and love."},{"q":"What happened after three months?","o":["She played at the school cultural day","She gave up","She broke the drum","Nothing"],"why":"Everyone clapped along."},{"q":"Galatians 6:9 says we shall reap in due season if we...?","o":["Faint not","Sleep more","Run away","Complain"],"why":"Don't be weary in well doing."}]}}},"mx2":{"challenge":[{"q":"What did Brother Lawrence say we can make our heart into?","o":["An oratory, a little chapel","A fortress","A shop","A garden wall"],"why":"To talk with God anywhere."},{"q":"\"Know ye not that ye are the ___ of God?\"","o":["temple","servants","children","friends"],"why":"1 Corinthians 3:16."},{"q":"What should you do before every task?","o":["Offer it to God","Complain","Check your phone","Sleep"],"why":"And thank Him after."},{"q":"\"Commit thy works unto the LORD, and thy thoughts shall be...\"","o":["established","forgotten","lost","changed"],"why":"Proverbs 16:3."},{"q":"Who prayed silently at Shiloh?","o":["Hannah","Bisola","Ruth","Esther"],"why":"Only her lips moved."},{"q":"Who was Hannah's son?","o":["Samuel","Saul","Solomon","Seth"],"why":"A great prophet."},{"q":"\"Let the words of my mouth, and the meditation of my ___...\"","o":["heart","friends","house","phone"],"why":"Psalm 19:14."},{"q":"What did Brother Lawrence compare the mind to?","o":["A garden","A library","A shop","A car"],"why":"Plant good seeds."},{"q":"Philippians 4:8 tells us to think on things that are...?","o":["True, honest, pure and lovely","Scary","Mean","Silly"],"why":"Fill your garden with those."},{"q":"\"Keep thy heart with all...\"","o":["diligence","money","friends","speed"],"why":"Proverbs 4:23."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Where was God's tabernacle when Hannah prayed?","o":["Shiloh","Jerusalem","Rome","Babylon"],"why":"Before the kings of Israel."},"choices":[{"title":"Far from church","q":"You're on holiday far from home, with no church nearby.","o":[{"t":"Step into the 'chapel' of your heart and talk with God there.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! You are God's temple wherever you go."},{"t":"Take a holiday from God too.","f":"God goes with you everywhere."},{"t":"Wait until you get home.","f":"Your heart-chapel is always open."}]},{"title":"Big test","q":"You're about to start a hard maths test.","o":[{"t":"Offer it to God first, do your best, and thank Him after.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Before and after, it's all for Him."},{"t":"Panic.","f":"Commit your work to the Lord."},{"t":"Only pray if it goes badly.","f":"Pray before, not just after."}]},{"title":"Silent room","q":"You're in a silent library and feel anxious. You can't speak.","o":[{"t":"Pray silently in your heart, like Hannah.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! God hears the words of your heart."},{"t":"Wait until you can pray out loud.","f":"Silent prayers count too."},{"t":"Leave the library.","f":"You can pray right where you are."}]},{"title":"Late-night scroll","q":"It's 11pm and you've been watching video after video. Some aren't good.","o":[{"t":"Turn it off, and fill your mind with something good.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Be the gatekeeper of your heart."},{"t":"Just a few more.","f":"Weeds grow fast."},{"t":"Keep watching, but feel bad.","f":"Guard your heart: act, don't just feel bad."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"cloister","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 2 of Spiritual Maxims in real life."},{"sc":"market","n":"⛪ Make your heart a chapel and visit it anywhere."},{"sc":"college","n":"🎁 Offer every task to God, and thank Him after."},{"sc":"temple","n":"🤫 God hears silent prayers from the heart."},{"sc":"home","n":"🛡️ Guard your heart. Watch what you let in."}],"stops":{"mx2s1":{"story":[{"sc":"college","w":"mxikenna","e":"worried","t":"I only really feel close to God at church on Sunday. The rest of the week, He feels far away."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"Ikenna, you don't have to be in a church building to be with God. In one of my letters I wrote that we can make our heart into a little chapel, an {oratory}."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"big","t":"You can slip into it at any moment, at school, on the bus, in the market, and talk with God there, quietly and lovingly."},{"sc":"cloister","n":"Paul taught the same thing: your body is God's temple, and His Spirit lives in you. Wherever you go, God's 'house' goes with you!"},{"sc":"market","w":"mxikenna","e":"smile","t":"So right here, in this busy market, I can step into my heart-chapel and talk to God?"},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"Yes! Close the door of your heart for a moment, and say, 'Lord, I'm here with You.'"},{"sc":"market","n":"Ikenna tried it, standing in the noisy market while his mum bought tomatoes. Just a few seconds. But he felt peace, right in the middle of the noise."}],"quote":{"text":"It is not necessary for being with God to be always at church; we may make an oratory of our heart, wherein to retire from time to time to converse with Him in meekness, humility, and love.","who":"From his Letters","tag":"Brother Lawrence's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Church in your heart","text":"Ikenna only felt close to God on Sundays. Brother Lawrence taught that you can make your heart a little chapel and step into it any time, anywhere. God's Spirit lives in you, so wherever you go, you can talk with Him."},"think":"Where is the busiest, noisiest place you go each week? Try stepping into your 'heart-chapel' there.","quiz":[{"q":"When did Ikenna usually feel close to God?","o":["Only at church on Sunday","All the time","Never","Only at school"],"why":"The rest of the week, God felt far."},{"q":"What did Brother Lawrence say we can make our heart into?","o":["A little chapel (an oratory)","A castle","A kitchen","A market"],"why":"To talk with God any time."},{"q":"What does 'oratory' mean?","o":["A small chapel for prayer","A speech","A kind of bread","A shop"],"why":"A quiet place for prayer."},{"q":"According to 1 Corinthians 3:16, what are we?","o":["The temple of God","Strangers","Kings","Servants of the market"],"why":"God's Spirit dwells in us."},{"q":"Where did Ikenna try his 'heart-chapel'?","o":["In a noisy market","In bed","At church","On a boat"],"why":"And he felt peace."}]},"mx2s2":{"story":[{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"Here's a simple practice from my maxims. Before you begin any task, offer it to God. When you finish, thank Him."},{"sc":"college","w":"mxbisola","e":"smirk","t":"Any task? Even homework?"},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"big","t":"Especially homework! Before: 'Lord, I'm doing this for You. Help me.' After: 'Thank You, Father.' It takes three seconds, and it turns the whole task into a gift for God."},{"sc":"college","n":"So Bisola tried it. Before her science homework: 'Lord, this is for You. Help me understand.' After: 'Thank You!'"},{"sc":"college","n":"Before football practice, Ikenna prayed: 'Lord, help me play fairly and well.' After: 'Thank You for my legs and lungs!'"},{"sc":"college","w":"mxikenna","e":"big","t":"It's like putting God's name on everything I do: 'Made for God'!"},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"And when you offer your work to God first, you'll find you work more carefully, more kindly and more peacefully."}],"quote":{"text":"In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths.","who":"Proverbs 3:6","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Offer it, then thank Him","text":"Brother Lawrence's practice: before any task, offer it to God; after, thank Him. It takes seconds, but it turns homework, chores and sport into gifts for God, and helps you work more carefully and peacefully."},"think":"Try 'before and after' prayers for every task tomorrow. How many can you remember?","quiz":[{"q":"What should you do before a task?","o":["Offer it to God","Complain","Check your phone","Nothing"],"why":"'Lord, I'm doing this for You.'"},{"q":"What should you do after a task?","o":["Thank God","Forget about it","Boast","Sleep"],"why":"'Thank You, Father.'"},{"q":"What did Bisola pray before science homework?","o":["'Lord, this is for You. Help me understand.'","Nothing","'Let it be easy'","'Do it for me'"],"why":"Then 'Thank You!'"},{"q":"What did Ikenna say it was like?","o":["Putting God's name on everything: 'Made for God'","A waste of time","Too hard","Boring"],"why":"Every task a gift."},{"q":"According to Proverbs 16:3, what should we commit to the LORD?","o":["Our works","Our money only","Nothing","Our enemies"],"why":"And our thoughts shall be established."}]},"mx2s3":{"story":[{"sc":"temple","n":"Long ago, a woman named Hannah was very sad. She longed for a child. Every year she went to the house of the LORD at {Shiloh}."},{"sc":"temple","n":"One year, she stood there and prayed with all her heart. But she didn't speak out loud. Her lips moved, but no sound came out."},{"sc":"temple","n":"Eli the priest was watching. He saw her lips moving with no sound, and thought something was wrong with her."},{"sc":"temple","w":"mxhannah","e":"worried","t":"No, my lord, I am a woman of a sorrowful spirit... I have poured out my soul before the LORD."},{"sc":"temple","w":"mxeli","e":"smile","t":"Go in peace: and the God of Israel grant thee thy petition that thou hast asked of him."},{"sc":"temple","n":"God heard Hannah's silent prayer. She had a son, Samuel, who grew up to be one of Israel's greatest prophets."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"You see? God hears the words of your heart, even when no one else can. In my maxims I encouraged short, simple prayers from the heart: 'My God, I am all Yours.' 'Lord, make me like You.'"},{"sc":"college","w":"mxbisola","e":"smile","t":"So in a quiet exam hall, I can still pray. Silently. And God hears!"}],"quote":{"text":"Now Hannah, she spake in her heart; only her lips moved, but her voice was not heard.","who":"1 Samuel 1:13","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"God hears your heart","text":"Hannah prayed silently, with only her lips moving, and God heard her. Brother Lawrence encouraged short, simple prayers from the heart, like 'My God, I am all Yours.' You can pray anywhere, even in a silent exam hall."},"think":"Make up your own short heart-prayer. Use it silently at least five times tomorrow.","quiz":[{"q":"What did Hannah long for?","o":["A child","Money","A house","A horse"],"why":"She was very sad."},{"q":"How did Hannah pray?","o":["Silently, with only her lips moving","Very loudly","In a song","She didn't pray"],"why":"1 Samuel 1:13."},{"q":"What did Eli think at first?","o":["That something was wrong with her","That she was singing","That she was asleep","That she was a prophet"],"why":"Then he blessed her."},{"q":"Who was Hannah's son?","o":["Samuel","David","Isaac","Joseph"],"why":"A great prophet."},{"q":"Which short prayer did Brother Lawrence suggest?","o":["'My God, I am all Yours'","'Give me everything'","'Hurry up'","'Not now'"],"why":"Simple prayers from the heart."}]},"mx2s4":{"story":[{"sc":"home","n":"Ikenna lay in bed scrolling through videos. One after another. Some were funny. Some were mean. Some were things his parents wouldn't want him to see."},{"sc":"home","w":"mxikenna","e":"worried","t":"I feel weird. Kind of empty and restless. And I can't stop thinking about some of those videos."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"Ikenna, my maxims taught that if we want to live close to God, we must guard our hearts. We have to watch what we let in."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"Your mind is like a garden. Whatever seeds you let in will grow. Plant weeds, and you'll get weeds. Plant good seeds, and you'll get flowers and fruit."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"big","t":"Paul said: whatsoever things are true, honest, just, pure, lovely and of good report, think on these things. Fill your garden with those."},{"sc":"home","w":"mxikenna","e":"smile","t":"So I need to be a gatekeeper. Not everything gets in."},{"sc":"home","n":"Ikenna deleted two apps that were filling his head with junk. He started charging his phone outside his room at night. A week later, he was sleeping better, and his mind felt clearer and calmer."}],"quote":{"text":"Whatsoever things are true, whatsoever things are honest, whatsoever things are just, whatsoever things are pure, whatsoever things are lovely... think on these things.","who":"Philippians 4:8","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Be the gatekeeper","text":"Ikenna felt empty after scrolling through junk. Brother Lawrence taught that to stay close to God, we must guard our hearts and watch what we let in. Your mind is a garden: plant good seeds, and think on what is true, pure and lovely."},"think":"What are you letting into your mind that's planting weeds? What could you replace it with?","quiz":[{"q":"How did Ikenna feel after scrolling for a long time?","o":["Empty and restless","Happy and rested","Strong","Sleepy and peaceful"],"why":"Some videos weren't good."},{"q":"What did Brother Lawrence say we must guard?","o":["Our hearts","Our money","Our shoes","Our phones only"],"why":"Watch what we let in."},{"q":"What did he compare the mind to?","o":["A garden","A river","A road","A clock"],"why":"Whatever seeds go in will grow."},{"q":"What did Ikenna do to guard his heart?","o":["Deleted junk apps and charged his phone outside his room","Watched more videos","Stopped sleeping","Nothing"],"why":"He slept better and felt calmer."},{"q":"According to Proverbs 4:23, what comes out of the heart?","o":["The issues of life","Nothing","Only bad things","Money"],"why":"Keep it with all diligence."}]}}},"mx3":{"challenge":[{"q":"Where did Jesus meet the Samaritan woman?","o":["At a well","On a mountain","In a boat","In a house"],"why":"John 4."},{"q":"What did Jesus offer her?","o":["Living water","A jar","Silver","Food"],"why":"The gift of God."},{"q":"\"God is a Spirit: and they that worship him must worship him in spirit and in...\"","o":["truth","church","Jerusalem","song"],"why":"John 4:24."},{"q":"Where was the people's heart when they honoured God only with their lips?","o":["Far from Him","Near Him","In the temple","Asleep"],"why":"Matthew 15:8."},{"q":"Which Yoruba proverb is about words?","o":["Many words don't fill a basket","Pride is a turban","Words are eggs","Patience cooks stones"],"why":"Ọ̀rọ̀ púpọ̀ kì í kún agbọ̀n."},{"q":"Who saw the Lord on a high throne?","o":["Isaiah","Ikenna","Hannah","Abraham"],"why":"Isaiah 6:1."},{"q":"\"Holy, holy, holy, is the LORD of...\"","o":["hosts","Israel","heaven","kings"],"why":"Isaiah 6:3."},{"q":"What did the seraph touch Isaiah's lips with?","o":["A live coal","A feather","A cup","A leaf"],"why":"And his sin was purged."},{"q":"\"Here am I; ___ me.\"","o":["send","help","save","leave"],"why":"Isaiah 6:8."},{"q":"Worship 'in truth' means seeing God as He is, and ourselves as...?","o":["We are","Better than others","Worthless","Perfect"],"why":"That's humility."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! How many wings did each seraph have?","o":["Six","Two","Four","Eight"],"why":"Isaiah 6:2."},"choices":[{"title":"Right place?","q":"A friend says, \"You can only really worship God in a big, beautiful church.\"","o":[{"t":"Kindly share that God is Spirit, and we can worship Him truly anywhere.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! In spirit and in truth, not in a special place."},{"t":"Agree and only worship at church.","f":"Jesus said it's not about the mountain or building."},{"t":"Argue loudly.","f":"Be gentle and kind."}]},{"title":"Empty singing","q":"You notice you're singing worship songs without thinking about the words.","o":[{"t":"Slow down and mean the words, even if you sing fewer.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Worship from the inside."},{"t":"Sing louder so people think you mean it.","f":"God looks at the heart, not the volume."},{"t":"Stop worshipping altogether.","f":"Just bring your heart back."}]},{"title":"Too big for God?","q":"Your problem feels too huge for God to handle.","o":[{"t":"Remember Isaiah's vision: God is holy, great, and on His throne.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! See God as He really is."},{"t":"Handle it alone.","f":"The whole earth is full of His glory. He can handle it."},{"t":"Give up.","f":"The LORD of hosts is bigger than any problem."}]},{"title":"Here am I","q":"Your youth pastor asks for volunteers to visit an orphanage. You feel unworthy.","o":[{"t":"Remember God's forgiveness and say, 'Here am I; send me.'","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Honest, forgiven, sent, like Isaiah."},{"t":"Stay quiet. You're not good enough.","f":"God cleanses and sends ordinary people."},{"t":"Volunteer just to look good.","f":"Go with a humble, willing heart."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"well","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 3 of Spiritual Maxims in real life."},{"sc":"well","n":"🏺 Worship God anywhere, in spirit and in truth."},{"sc":"church","n":"💓 Mean what you sing and pray."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"👑 See God as He really is: holy and great."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"🙋 See yourself honestly, receive forgiveness, and say 'Here am I.'"}],"stops":{"mx3s1":{"story":[{"sc":"well","n":"One hot day in {Samaria}, Jesus sat down by a well, tired from His journey. A woman came at noon to draw water, alone."},{"sc":"well","w":"mxjesus","e":"smile","t":"Give me to drink."},{"sc":"well","w":"mxwoman","e":"shock","t":"How is it that thou, being a Jew, askest drink of me, which am a woman of Samaria?"},{"sc":"well","w":"mxjesus","e":"smile","t":"If thou knewest the gift of God, and who it is that saith to thee, Give me to drink; thou wouldest have asked of him, and he would have given thee living water."},{"sc":"well","n":"They talked. The woman asked which mountain was the right place to worship God: hers in Samaria, or the temple in Jerusalem?"},{"sc":"well","w":"mxjesus","e":"big","t":"God is a Spirit: and they that worship him must worship him in spirit and in truth."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"Some of my maxims are about these very words. Worshipping God isn't about the right building or the right mountain. It's about your heart meeting God, honestly, wherever you are."},{"sc":"well","n":"The woman ran back to her town and told everyone about Jesus. Many came out to meet Him and believed."}],"quote":{"text":"If thou knewest the gift of God, and who it is that saith to thee, Give me to drink; thou wouldest have asked of him, and he would have given thee living water.","who":"John 4:10","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Worship isn't about a place","text":"The woman at the well wanted to know the right place to worship. Jesus said God is Spirit, and true worshippers worship in spirit and truth. Brother Lawrence's maxims teach the same: worship is your heart meeting God honestly, wherever you are."},"think":"Where have you felt closest to God? Could you worship Him just as truly in your bedroom or classroom?","quiz":[{"q":"Where did Jesus meet the woman?","o":["At a well in Samaria","In the temple","On a boat","In a market"],"why":"On a hot day at noon."},{"q":"What did Jesus ask her for?","o":["A drink","Money","Bread","Directions"],"why":"\"Give me to drink.\""},{"q":"What did Jesus offer her?","o":["Living water","Gold","A new jar","A house"],"why":"John 4:10."},{"q":"How must true worshippers worship God?","o":["In spirit and in truth","Only on mountains","Only in Jerusalem","Only loudly"],"why":"John 4:24."},{"q":"What did the woman do afterwards?","o":["Told her whole town about Jesus","Hid","Went to Jerusalem","Forgot about it"],"why":"Many believed."}]},"mx3s2":{"story":[{"sc":"church","n":"At church, Ikenna sang all the songs. Loudly. But he was thinking about football the whole time. He didn't mean a single word."},{"sc":"church","w":"mxikenna","e":"smirk","t":"Well, at least I sang. That counts, right?"},{"sc":"temple","n":"Jesus once spoke to some religious leaders who were very good at saying the right things, but whose hearts were far from God. He quoted the prophet Isaiah."},{"sc":"temple","w":"mxjesus","e":"stern","t":"This people draweth nigh unto me with their mouth, and honoureth me with their lips; but their heart is far from me."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"In spirit means worship comes from the inside, from your spirit, not just your lips. God isn't impressed by loud singing if the heart is empty."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"big","t":"But even one quiet word, meant with your whole heart, is real worship. God looks at the heart."},{"sc":"church","n":"The next Sunday, Ikenna listened to the words as he sang. When they sang 'I love You, Lord,' he stopped and asked himself: do I? Then he sang it again, and this time he meant it."}],"quote":{"text":"This people draweth nigh unto me with their mouth, and honoureth me with their lips; but their heart is far from me.","who":"Matthew 15:8","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Mean what you sing","text":"Ikenna sang loudly but meant nothing. Jesus warned about people who honour God with their lips while their hearts are far away. True worship comes from the inside. Even one word meant with your whole heart is real worship."},"think":"Next time you sing or pray at church, slow down and ask: do I mean this?","proverb":{"text":"Ọ̀rọ̀ púpọ̀ kì í kún agbọ̀n.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"Many words don't fill a basket. It's not how much you say that counts, but what's real."},"quiz":[{"q":"What was Ikenna thinking about while singing?","o":["Football","The words","God","His homework"],"why":"He didn't mean a word."},{"q":"Who did Jesus quote about lip-service?","o":["Isaiah","Moses","David","Paul"],"why":"Matthew 15:8."},{"q":"Where was the people's heart, according to Jesus?","o":["Far from God","Close to God","In the temple","In heaven"],"why":"They honoured Him only with their lips."},{"q":"What does 'in spirit' mean, according to Brother Lawrence?","o":["Worship from the inside, not just the lips","Singing loudly","Worshipping only at night","Using big words"],"why":"God looks at the heart."},{"q":"What does the Yoruba proverb say many words don't fill?","o":["A basket","A pot","A house","A boat"],"why":"What's real matters more."}]},"mx3s3":{"story":[{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"In truth means seeing God as He really is. Not a small god in a box. Not a grumpy old man. The real, living, holy God."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"The prophet Isaiah once saw a vision. The Lord sat on a throne, high and lifted up, and the hem of His robe filled the temple."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"Around Him flew shining {seraphim}. Each had six wings. With two they covered their faces, with two their feet, and with two they flew."},{"sc":"throneglory","w":"mxseraph","e":"big","t":"Holy, holy, holy, is the LORD of hosts: the whole earth is full of his glory."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"The doorposts shook at the sound, and the house was filled with smoke."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"big","t":"When you see God as He truly is, so holy, so great, so beautiful, worship comes naturally. You can't help it!"},{"sc":"college","w":"mxbisola","e":"smile","t":"Sometimes I think of God as small, like He can't handle my problems. But He's the LORD of hosts, and the whole earth is full of His glory!"}],"quote":{"text":"I saw also the Lord sitting upon a throne, high and lifted up, and his train filled the temple.","who":"Isaiah 6:1","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"See how great He is","text":"Worshipping 'in truth' means seeing God as He really is. Isaiah saw the Lord on a high throne, with seraphim crying 'Holy, holy, holy!' When you see how great, holy and beautiful God is, worship comes naturally."},"think":"Do you sometimes think of God as too small for your problems? What does Isaiah's vision show you?","quiz":[{"q":"What does worshipping 'in truth' mean, according to Brother Lawrence?","o":["Seeing God as He really is","Never telling lies","Worshipping in a building","Singing old songs"],"why":"Not a small god in a box."},{"q":"Where did Isaiah see the Lord sitting?","o":["On a throne, high and lifted up","In a boat","Under a tree","In a kitchen"],"why":"Isaiah 6:1."},{"q":"How many wings did each seraph have?","o":["Six","Two","Four","Ten"],"why":"To cover face, feet, and fly."},{"q":"What did the seraphim cry?","o":["Holy, holy, holy","Hurry, hurry","Hello","Peace, peace"],"why":"Isaiah 6:3."},{"q":"What is the whole earth full of?","o":["His glory","Fear","Money","Noise"],"why":"Isaiah 6:3."}]},"mx3s4":{"story":[{"sc":"throneglory","w":"mxisaiah","e":"worried","t":"Woe is me! for I am undone; because I am a man of unclean lips, and I dwell in the midst of a people of unclean lips."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"When Isaiah saw how holy God is, he also saw himself clearly: a sinner. But God didn't leave him there."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"One of the seraphim flew to him with a live coal from the altar and touched his lips."},{"sc":"throneglory","w":"mxseraph","e":"smile","t":"Lo, this hath touched thy lips; and thine iniquity is taken away, and thy sin purged."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"Then Isaiah heard the voice of the Lord: 'Whom shall I send, and who will go for us?'"},{"sc":"throneglory","w":"mxisaiah","e":"big","t":"Here am I; send me."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"This is the other half of 'in truth': seeing ourselves as we really are. Not pretending to be better, and not hating ourselves either. That's {humility}."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"big","t":"See God as He is, see yourself as you are, receive His forgiveness, and then say, 'Here am I; send me.'"}],"quote":{"text":"Lo, this hath touched thy lips; and thine iniquity is taken away, and thy sin purged.","who":"Isaiah 6:7","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Honest, forgiven, sent","text":"When Isaiah saw God's holiness, he saw his own sin. God cleansed him, then Isaiah said, 'Here am I; send me.' Worship in truth means seeing God as He is, and ourselves as we are, with humility. Then we're ready to be sent."},"think":"What would it mean for you to say 'Here am I; send me' to God this week?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Isaiah say when he saw God's holiness?","o":["\"Woe is me! for I am undone\"","\"Hooray!\"","\"I'm perfect\"","Nothing"],"why":"He saw his own sin."},{"q":"What touched Isaiah's lips?","o":["A live coal from the altar","Water","Honey","Bread"],"why":"Brought by a seraph."},{"q":"What happened to Isaiah's sin?","o":["It was taken away","It stayed","It got worse","It was ignored"],"why":"Isaiah 6:7."},{"q":"What did Isaiah say when God asked, 'Whom shall I send?'","o":["\"Here am I; send me\"","\"Send someone else\"","\"Not now\"","\"I'm busy\""],"why":"Isaiah 6:8."},{"q":"What is humility, according to Brother Lawrence?","o":["Seeing ourselves as we really are","Hating ourselves","Pretending to be great","Being shy"],"why":"Not better, not worse."}]}}},"mx4":{"challenge":[{"q":"Who walked on water towards Jesus?","o":["Peter","Cleopas","Isaiah","Abraham"],"why":"Matthew 14."},{"q":"Why did Peter start to sink?","o":["He looked at the storm","He was too heavy","He couldn't swim","Jesus let go"],"why":"Eyes off Jesus."},{"q":"\"Without faith it is impossible to ___ him.\"","o":["please","see","find","hear"],"why":"Hebrews 11:6."},{"q":"\"Why art thou cast down, O my...\"","o":["soul","friend","king","people"],"why":"Psalm 42."},{"q":"What did the psalm writer tell his soul?","o":["Hope thou in God","Give up","Run away","Be angry"],"why":"I shall yet praise Him."},{"q":"Which village were the two disciples walking to?","o":["Emmaus","Bethany","Nazareth","Jericho"],"why":"Luke 24."},{"q":"\"Did not our heart ___ within us?\"","o":["burn","break","sink","sleep"],"why":"Luke 24:32."},{"q":"When did the disciples recognise Jesus at Emmaus?","o":["When He broke the bread","On the road","At the gate","Never"],"why":"Their eyes were opened."},{"q":"\"In thy presence is fulness of...\"","o":["joy","fear","silence","work"],"why":"Psalm 16:11."},{"q":"Jesus spoke so that His joy might be...?","o":["In us, and full","Hidden","Small","Forgotten"],"why":"John 15:11."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What was the name of one of the two disciples on the road to Emmaus?","o":["Cleopas","Thomas","Stephen","Barnabas"],"why":"Luke 24:18."},"choices":[{"title":"Storm-staring","q":"Exams, family troubles and a falling-out with a friend. You can't stop thinking about it all.","o":[{"t":"Turn your eyes to Jesus: pray, and trust Him with each thing.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Eyes on Jesus, not the storm."},{"t":"Keep staring at the problems.","f":"That's when Peter began to sink."},{"t":"Pretend nothing's wrong.","f":"Cry out like Peter: 'Lord, save me!'"}]},{"title":"Big disappointment","q":"You weren't picked for something you really wanted.","o":[{"t":"Be honest with God, then tell your soul: hope in God.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! I shall yet praise Him."},{"t":"Decide nothing will ever work out.","f":"Disappointment isn't the end of the story."},{"t":"Blame everyone else.","f":"Bring it to God instead."}]},{"title":"Cold heart","q":"Your love for God feels cold and dull lately.","o":[{"t":"Spend time walking and talking with Jesus, and reading His word.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Hearts burn when He talks with us by the way."},{"t":"Wait for a big feeling to come.","f":"Time with Him warms the heart."},{"t":"Give up on God.","f":"He's walking beside you, even when you don't recognise Him."}]},{"title":"Joy thief","q":"You think you'll only be happy when you get the newest phone.","o":[{"t":"Remember real joy comes from God's presence, not things.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! In His presence is fulness of joy."},{"t":"Beg until you get it.","f":"Things never give lasting joy."},{"t":"Be miserable until then.","f":"Joy is available today, with God."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"cloister","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Spiritual Maxims in real life."},{"sc":"nightsea","n":"🌊 Keep your eyes on Jesus, not the storm."},{"sc":"night","n":"🌤️ Talk to your soul: hope in God!"},{"sc":"emmaus","n":"🔥 Walk and talk with Jesus, and your heart will burn."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"😊 Real joy is found in His presence."}],"stops":{"mx4s1":{"story":[{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"My last maxims are about the gifts God gives when we live in His presence. The first gift: our faith comes alive."},{"sc":"nightsea","n":"One stormy night, Jesus' disciples were in a boat, battling the wind and waves. Then they saw Jesus walking towards them on the water!"},{"sc":"nightsea","w":"mxpeter","e":"shock","t":"Lord, if it be thou, bid me come unto thee on the water."},{"sc":"nightsea","w":"mxjesus","e":"smile","t":"Come."},{"sc":"nightsea","n":"Peter climbed out and walked on the water towards Jesus! But then he looked at the wind and the waves. He was afraid, and began to sink."},{"sc":"nightsea","w":"mxpeter","e":"worried","t":"Lord, save me!"},{"sc":"nightsea","w":"mxjesus","e":"smile","t":"O thou of little faith, wherefore didst thou doubt?"},{"sc":"nightsea","n":"Immediately Jesus reached out His hand and caught him."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"big","t":"While Peter's eyes were on Jesus, he walked on water. When he looked at the storm, he sank. Living in God's presence keeps our eyes on Him, and that keeps our faith alive."}],"quote":{"text":"And immediately Jesus stretched forth his hand, and caught him, and said unto him, O thou of little faith, wherefore didst thou doubt?","who":"Matthew 14:31","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Eyes on Jesus","text":"Peter walked on water while he looked at Jesus, and sank when he looked at the storm. Even then, Jesus caught him. Brother Lawrence taught that living in God's presence keeps our eyes on Him, and that makes our faith come alive."},"think":"What 'storm' are you staring at right now? How could you turn your eyes back to Jesus?","quiz":[{"q":"What did the disciples see on the stormy night?","o":["Jesus walking on the water","A ghost ship","A whale","A lighthouse"],"why":"Matthew 14."},{"q":"What one word did Jesus say to Peter?","o":["\"Come\"","\"Stay\"","\"Swim\"","\"Wait\""],"why":"And Peter walked on water!"},{"q":"Why did Peter begin to sink?","o":["He looked at the wind and waves and was afraid","The water was too deep","He was tired","He tripped"],"why":"His eyes left Jesus."},{"q":"What did Jesus do when Peter cried out?","o":["Caught him immediately","Let him sink","Laughed","Walked away"],"why":"Matthew 14:31."},{"q":"According to Hebrews 11:6, what is impossible without faith?","o":["To please God","To swim","To sleep","To eat"],"why":"Believe that He is."}]},"mx4s2":{"story":[{"sc":"home","n":"Bisola didn't get into the school choir. She had practised for weeks. Now she felt completely {cast down}."},{"sc":"home","w":"mxbisola","e":"worried","t":"What's the point of trying? Nothing ever works out for me."},{"sc":"night","n":"Long ago, a psalm writer felt just like that. He was far from home, people mocked him, and he felt God had forgotten him. So he talked to himself honestly."},{"sc":"night","n":"'Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him.'"},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"Notice what he did, Bisola. He didn't pretend he was fine. But he told his own soul: hope in God! I shall YET praise Him. The story isn't over."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"big","t":"That's the second gift of God's presence: hope grows strong. When you know He's with you, even disappointment can't take your hope away."},{"sc":"home","w":"mxbisola","e":"smile","t":"Okay, soul. Listen. Hope in God. I'll try again next year. And I'll keep singing in the meantime, for Him."}],"quote":{"text":"Why art thou cast down, O my soul? and why art thou disquieted within me? hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him.","who":"Psalm 42:11","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Talk to your soul","text":"When the psalm writer felt cast down, he spoke to his own soul: 'Hope thou in God: I shall yet praise Him.' Brother Lawrence taught that God's presence makes hope grow strong. Disappointment isn't the end of the story."},"think":"What disappointment are you carrying? Try talking to your own soul like the psalm writer did.","quiz":[{"q":"Why was Bisola cast down?","o":["She didn't get into the choir","She lost her shoes","She was hungry","She was late"],"why":"After weeks of practice."},{"q":"What does 'cast down' mean?","o":["Feeling low and discouraged","Throwing something","Sitting down","Being happy"],"why":"The psalm writer felt it too."},{"q":"Who did the psalm writer talk to?","o":["His own soul","A king","A friend","A priest"],"why":"\"Why art thou cast down, O my soul?\""},{"q":"What did he tell his soul to do?","o":["Hope in God","Give up","Run away","Stop praying"],"why":"For I shall yet praise Him."},{"q":"What gift of God's presence is this stop about?","o":["Hope grows strong","Getting rich","Never feeling sad","Winning every contest"],"why":"Disappointment isn't the end."}]},"mx4s3":{"story":[{"sc":"emmaus","n":"Three days after Jesus died, two of His followers were walking sadly home to the village of {Emmaus}. One was called Cleopas."},{"sc":"emmaus","n":"A stranger joined them on the road. It was Jesus, risen from the dead! But they didn't recognise Him."},{"sc":"emmaus","w":"mxcleopas","e":"worried","t":"We trusted that it had been he which should have redeemed Israel. But they crucified him..."},{"sc":"emmaus","n":"As they walked, the stranger explained the Scriptures to them, from Moses and all the prophets, showing them everything about the Messiah."},{"sc":"emmaus","n":"At the village, they invited Him to stay. At supper, He took bread, blessed it, broke it and gave it to them. Suddenly their eyes were opened: it was Jesus! And then He vanished from their sight."},{"sc":"emmaus","w":"mxcleopas","e":"big","t":"Did not our heart burn within us, while he talked with us by the way?"},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"big","t":"That's the third gift! When we walk with Jesus and talk with Him, our love for Him catches fire. The more time in His presence, the warmer our hearts become."},{"sc":"emmaus","n":"That very hour, the two ran all the way back to Jerusalem in the dark to tell the others: 'The Lord is risen indeed!'"}],"quote":{"text":"And it came to pass, that, while they communed together and reasoned, Jesus himself drew near, and went with them.","who":"Luke 24:15","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Walk with Him, burn for Him","text":"Two sad disciples walked with Jesus without knowing it, and their hearts burned as He talked with them. Brother Lawrence taught that time in God's presence sets our love for Him on fire. Walk and talk with Jesus every day."},"think":"When have you felt your heart 'burn' with love for God? What helped it happen?","quiz":[{"q":"Where were the two followers walking?","o":["To Emmaus","To Rome","To Bethlehem","To Egypt"],"why":"About seven miles from Jerusalem."},{"q":"Who joined them on the road?","o":["The risen Jesus","An angel","A soldier","Peter"],"why":"But they didn't recognise Him."},{"q":"When did they recognise Jesus?","o":["When He broke bread at supper","On the road","In the morning","Never"],"why":"Their eyes were opened."},{"q":"What did they say about their hearts?","o":["They burned within them","They were cold","They were broken","They were empty"],"why":"Luke 24:32."},{"q":"What did the two do that very hour?","o":["Ran back to Jerusalem to tell the others","Went to bed","Stayed in Emmaus","Hid"],"why":"The Lord is risen indeed!"}]},"mx4s4":{"story":[{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"smile","t":"And the last gift? Joy. Deep, quiet joy that doesn't depend on whether things are easy or hard."},{"sc":"monkkitchen","n":"Brother Lawrence spent his life in a kitchen and a sandal workshop. He had a bad leg, little money, and no fame. Yet everyone who met him noticed his joy."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"big","t":"Where did it come from? Not from my circumstances. From His presence! The psalm says: in thy presence is fulness of joy."},{"sc":"upperroom","n":"On the night before He died, Jesus told His disciples why He'd taught them so much."},{"sc":"upperroom","w":"mxjesus","e":"smile","t":"These things have I spoken unto you, that my joy might remain in you, and that your joy might be full."},{"sc":"college","w":"mxikenna","e":"smile","t":"So Brother Lawrence's maxims all lead to the same place: believe, hope, love, practise God's presence... and find real joy."},{"sc":"cloister","w":"mxlawrence","e":"big","t":"Yes! Now, my young friends, why not write a few maxims of your own? Short sayings to help you remember God all day. Then live them!"},{"sc":"college","w":"mxbisola","e":"big","t":"Here's mine: 'At the sink or on the stage, God is with me.'"},{"sc":"college","w":"mxikenna","e":"big","t":"And mine: 'Eyes on Jesus, not the storm!'"}],"quote":{"text":"These things have I spoken unto you, that my joy might remain in you, and that your joy might be full.","who":"John 15:11","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Joy in His presence","text":"Brother Lawrence had little money, a bad leg and no fame, yet he was full of joy, because joy comes from God's presence, not our circumstances. Jesus wants His joy to be in you, full. Write your own maxims, and live them."},"think":"Write two or three short maxims of your own to help you remember God every day. Where will you put them?","quiz":[{"q":"What was the last gift Brother Lawrence named?","o":["Joy","Money","Fame","Strength"],"why":"Deep, quiet joy."},{"q":"Where did his joy come from?","o":["God's presence","His riches","His fame","An easy life"],"why":"Not from his circumstances."},{"q":"According to Psalm 16:11, what is in God's presence?","o":["Fulness of joy","Fear","Sadness","Nothing"],"why":"And pleasures for evermore."},{"q":"Why did Jesus say He'd spoken to His disciples?","o":["That His joy might remain in them","To scare them","To test them","To fill time"],"why":"John 15:11."},{"q":"What did Brother Lawrence invite you to do at the end?","o":["Write your own maxims and live them","Become a monk","Learn to cook","Forget everything"],"why":"Short sayings to remember God."}]}}}});
